{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Gather for Me seventy men.</b> What is 'for Me' and what is 'men' — why not say 'אנשים'? Rather, specific ones, as it were, who are like Me, as it is said: ״YHWH is a man of war״; and who are like you, as it is said: ״and the man Moses was very humble״; and so we expound in Sanhedrin: 'with you' — like you. Another explanation: 'for Me' — that they sustain My heaven and My earth, as it is said: ״He who builds His upper chambers in heaven, and His agudah on earth He founded״ — for the sake of My agudah, of the Sanhedrin, the earth is founded. And if there is no earth, there is no heaven — a parable to a great palace built upon ships: as long as the ships are joined together, the palace upon them stands; the ships were removed — the palace fell." "<b>Whom you know.</b> For they are the ones who were beaten on their account in Egypt, as it is said: ״ויכו שוטרי בני ישראל״. Anyone who delivers himself over for Israel merits greatness, honor, and the holy spirit."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:10.940907902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}